      "writtenOn": "2021-02-05T16:05:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what you mean about `String` being immutable; strings aren\u0027t any more or less mutable than any other type in Rust. Removed in anyway, I\u0027m not quite sure what difference it makes, it just seemed to be what other AIDL files do.\n\nDavid had the same concern. The current config file is just a placeholder until I figure out how to integrate with the Cuttlefish tools, but they currently use JSON for quite a lot. I don\u0027t think using a Parcelable would really solve the problem of file visibility, because there will also be a bunch of other files that need to be visible (the various disk images, for a start).",
      "parentUuid": "c68f61f4_7ec680b8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "6a45c9beca3d7415d20d0bd63c5c79a38e83b519",
